# Every attribute a driver classifies IMMUTABLE, as service|attribute|state.
#
# `immutable` is not an opinion about how fundamental something feels: it tells the
# compiler an in-place change is impossible, so the plan carries a DESTROY AND
# RECREATE. It is therefore a claim about the PROVIDER's API, and only the provider
# can settle it — D806 found one that its own documentation contradicts in a
# sentence, and the cost of it was a budget deleted to change its period.
#
# A line is `checked: <what said so>` or `unchecked`. The gate holds two things:
# every claim in the code appears here (a new one cannot arrive unnoticed), and the
# number of unchecked lines may only go DOWN — the debt-list idiom of
# knownNoAdoptRead, which cannot rot into a set of stale excuses.
#
# Auditing the rest is the work D806 named. It is not a footnote to a fix.
aws/ACM|location.region|checked: no Update*/Modify*/Put*/Set* operation in any of the 43 botocore models this repo calls accepts a region — a resource's region is part of its ARN
